id: pm-pznhee
title: "MCP Apps for pm: interactive graph, context, plan, assurance, and long-operation views with consent-safe action boundaries"
description: Expose optional interactive pm views as MCP Apps while keeping authoritative state and mutations in SDK-backed tools and resources.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[8]: "area:mcp",assurance,context,graph,interaction,long-term,mcp-apps,visualization
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:11:42.545Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-26T16:57:28.931Z"
deadline: "2027-06-30T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-26T16:57:28.244Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-26T16:57:28.244Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 1200
acceptance_criteria: "Each app reads authoritative SDK resources and never becomes a second tracker or mutable cache of record; All mutations use declared MCP tools with preview, consent, authority, idempotency, and immutable receipts; Graph and context explanations preserve typed edges, provenance, omissions, confidence, and token accounting; Accessibility, keyboard operation, reduced motion, large graphs, degraded connections, and stale data have explicit tests; Apps are optional extensions and absence never removes core CLI, SDK, or MCP functionality"
goal: Interactive context without creating a second project-management state
objective: "Render graph exploration, context selection, plan progress, assurance verdicts, and task state through standard MCP App contracts"
value: Humans and agents can inspect complex project relationships and evidence interactively while preserving one immutable source of truth
why_now: "MCP Apps are a notable extension and pm already owns graph, context, plans, tasks, and assurance primitives that benefit from safe interactive presentation"
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: high
confidence: low
resolution: Delivered five SDK-owned MCP App contracts with negotiated tool/resource projection and self-contained accessible views.
expected_result: Optional interactive context views preserve the SDK and pm tracker as the only authoritative state while core MCP remains available without Apps.
actual_result: "Context, graph, plan, assurance, and operation contracts use official metadata shapes, zero external permissions, bounded rendering, graceful optional discovery, strict resource access, and packed npx/bunx proof without leaking upstream declaration defects."
