comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:11:42.545Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for MCP Apps interactive graph context plan assurance and task views. Existing graph and context owners provide primitives but no standard MCP App presentation layer."
  "2026-08-26T15:49:44.251Z","harness:codex","Final implementation evidence: five SDK-owned stable MCP Apps views decorate existing tools only after explicit 2026-01-26 negotiation; self-contained ui:// resources use the official MIME and metadata contracts, zero network/storage/device permissions, accessible responsive rendering, bounded output, host handshake, cancellation/context events, and text fallback. The UI/core deprecation boundary gate, final exact 8,011-test 100/100/100/100 run, full static quality, package artifact, and fresh npx/bunx/MCP packed consumer all passed."
  "2026-08-26T16:57:16.640Z","harness:codex","PR review remediation evidence: optional incompatible Apps declarations now degrade only tools/list and resources/list to the core surface; explicit app reads and unexpected internal failures remain fail-closed. Official ext-apps types remain a development-time conformance oracle without leaking its invalid NodeNext declarations into published pm SDK types. Public surface snapshot is unchanged; packed external TypeScript, npx, bunx, and app HTML reads passed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T15:49:41.774Z","harness:codex","MCP Apps has its own stable UI protocol namespace: ui/notifications/initialized is required extension vocabulary and must not be classified as the removed core notifications/initialized method."
